  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fig 13, 'DIIG digital health enterprise architecture framework'. Within the enterprise, a digital health platform holds shared services (business domain and registry services such as terminology, client, facility, product and health worker registries), data sources (institution-based and population-based) and data services (analytics, dashboards, repositories), joined by an interoperability layer of enabling components. Point-of-service applications below are reused across programmes or used for one use case only; external non-health systems sit to the right; a legend marks investment types. Adapted from the 2020 WHO Digital Implementation Investment Guide.",
